A||||5||Smokin87||bad gas cap?||||5||
Z||000000||Smokin87||01-31-2001||04:32 PM||||Recently i have had problems with my car.  I fixed them...i think.  Now when i am driving, the check engine light comes on.  and it goes off when i turn the car off.  I'm pretty sure i have a bad gas cap, but will this make the engine light go on.  i thought this car was too old (87) to have a gas pressure sensor.  also, is there a way i can read the code without hooking the car up to a computer?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_copy.jpg">  <BR>"When man wanted to make the car faster...he invented the jet-plane."||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||01-31-2001||05:11 PM||||yes there is a way to check it. you just need to get a paper clip or something similar. take off the black cigarette trim on the console. you'll see the inlet, or whatever it's called, to the computer. have your car on, but not running. take your paper clip and connect the two on the bottom right, facing the front. or it would be bottom left if you're looking to the back of the car. this will blink a code with your check engine light. it will blink the 12 code 3 times, then if you have a problem code, it will blink 3 times after that.<BR>phew, i think that's covered it all. someone correct me if i'm wrong on the procedure.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-31-2001||11:41 PM||||Fiero does not know anything about fuel tank pressure or cap etc. That's an OBDII thing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||02-01-2001||02:41 AM||||Smokin87, it is normal for the light to go out when you turn the car off - everything goes off then.........I would suspect one of the many sensors on the engine - normally it is in the EGR system somewhere (valve, tube, solenoid) or could even be a coolant sensor - are there any other symptoms of a problem? I really don't think a bad gas cap (how does a gas cap go bad?) will cause you any problems - NO gas cap will not normally cause a problem other than gas evaporation.......<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">    </A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smokin87||02-01-2001||04:47 PM||||there is no problem with the car.  just sometimes the check engine light comes on.  and when i turn the car off and on again it is gone.  Like, yesterday i left my house, drove 5 minutes to a gas station.  about 3 minutes into the trip the check engine light went on.  when i got to the gas station, i turned the car off.  i filled up, then when i turned the car on again, the light went off and stayed off the whole way home.  this happens alot.  and i thought it might be a bad gas cap because when i take the cap off there is no "hiss" sound.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_copy.jpg">  <BR>"When man wanted to make the car faster...he invented the jet-plane."||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||02-01-2001||07:46 PM||||it sounds like a coolant sensor to me -- light comes on when the temp heats up....I had that happen to me once -- there are two coolant sensors, by the way - the one which usually gives you a problem like you described can be found under the oil sending unit on the forward right side of the engine block....||||reg||1
